# In-process and working files, including the message a commit is given with
# -F. Gitignored so that naming it on the command line can never put it into
# the commit it describes.
.ephemera/

# Session entry point: ephemeral by design, rewritten each session.
START_HERE.md

# Python's caches. This repository's own Python went with the port; what is
# left is the checkers linked in from toolbox, which run from here and leave
# their caches here. Both entries carry a `.gitignore` holding `*` that the
# tool writes itself, so a cache hides from `git status` on its own account and
# these lines are belt to that brace.
__pycache__/

# Adopted jig links, and the run directories they produce. The links resolve
# into toolbox; in a built image the same files arrive from the anvil layer
# beneath, so a committed copy would be a third statement of one thing.
#
# MATCHED BY SHAPE. The objection recorded here was to `bolt.*.yaml`, which does
# swallow `bolt.go-std-quality.definitions.yaml` — this project's own values for
# the shared jig's placeholders, which has to be committed. `bolt.*-quality.yaml`
# is the narrower form and cannot match a `*.definitions.yaml`, so the objection
# was to the wrong glob rather than to globbing at all. skid has used this form
# throughout; bolt and qwark carry it as of 2026-09-04.
#
# A pattern covers a set that grows and a list does not. bolt adopted toolbox's
# `rust` set on 2026-09-03 and left two links untracked, because adopting a set
# and editing five .gitignore files are different acts and only the first is
# forced.
#
# `config/` holds one link and none of this project's own settings. The Go jig
# names `{config_dir}/config/go-std-quality.golangci.yml`, and `config_dir` is
# the project root, so an adopter links the shared file in at that path.
bolt.*-quality.yaml
bolt.secrets.yaml
adapters/
config/

# Run directories. A run's artefacts belong to the run rather than the repo, and
# the stamp format changed with the Rust build, so both are covered.
.bolt-*/
.bolt*/

# Adopted checker scripts, linked into bin/ from toolbox.
bin/*.py

.ruff_cache/

# The built binaries. bin/infobot and bin/forget-session are committed shims
# that exec these; an absent binary is reported rather than rendering blank,
# which is FR-1.13 and the reason the shims are the committed half.
bin/statusline
bin/forget


# Zig build output, from an implementation retired at 2c19f0b. Kept ignored
# because a rebuild of that tree must not land binaries here.
zig/
